rates can slow down these activities.^A lower rate increases the money supply, while a higher rate restricts it.^Lower rates can lead to bullish market trends, while higher rates might cause bearish sentiment.^The trends in the repo rate helps to assess the central bank's monetary policy stance and the correlation between key economic indicators such as GDP growth, inflation rates, and demand for bank credit."}],"related":[{"slug":"aggregate-bank-deposits","title":"Aggregate Bank Deposits"},{"slug":"bank-credit-industry","title":"Bank Credit - Industry"},{"slug":"bank-credit-personal-loans","title":"Bank Credit - Personal Loans"},{"slug":"bank-credit-services","title":"Bank Credit - Services"},{"slug":"cash-reserve-ratio-crr","title":"Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)"},{"slug":"credit-deposit-ratio","title":"Credit-Deposit Ratio"},{"slug":"foreign-exchange-reserves","title":"Foreign Exchange Reserves"},{"slug":"foreign-portfolio-investments-fpis-debt","title":"Foreign Portfolio Investments (FPIs) - Debt"},{"slug":"marginal-cost-of-funds-based-lending-rates-mclr","title":"Marginal Cost of Funds based Lending Rates (MCLR)"},{"slug":"money-supply-m3","title":"Money Supply (M3)"},{"slug":"nifty-bank-pe-ratio","title":"NIFTY Bank P/E Ratio"},{"slug":"rbi-liquidity-net-laf","title":"RBI Liquidity (Net LAF)"},{"slug":"statutory-liquidity-ratio-slr","title":"Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR)"},{"slug":"term-deposit-rate","title":"Term Deposit Rate"},{"slug":"weighted-average-lending-rate-on-fresh-rupee-loans-walr","title":"Weighted Average Lending Rate on Fresh Rupee Loans (WALR)"}],"title":"Repo Rate","description":"The current RBI repo rate is 5.50% as of 25 Oct, 2026, the rate at which the RBI lends to commercial banks in India. The RBI repo rate today shapes loan EMIs, deposit rates, and the overall direction of India's monetary policy.","headline":{"Absolute":"The current RBI repo rate is 5.50% as of 25 Oct, 2026, the rate at which the RBI lends to commercial banks in India. The RBI repo rate today shapes loan EMIs, deposit rates, and the overall direction of India's monetary policy."},"source":null,"source_url":null,"date_modified":"2026-10-25","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T06:10:16+00:00"}